            <ArticleTitle>Polytetrafluoroethylene vs. polypropylene suture for endoscopic bladder neck suspension.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>119-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Between May 1989 and October 1989, 24 women underwent a prospective, randomized study comparing polypropylene (Prolene) and polytetrafluoroethylene (Gore-Tex) sutures for endoscopic bladder neck suspension. Polypropylene was associated with significantly more suture pain than polytetrafluoroethylene. Polytetrafluoroethylene was more difficult to tie at a predetermined tension.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
